---
import ComponentPage from '../../layouts/component-page.astro';

const html = `<!-- In the region's content: a pressed toggle is a cursor block -->
<div role="group" aria-label="View">
  <button type="button" class="nib-button nib-button--outline" aria-pressed="true">GRID</button>
  <button type="button" class="nib-button nib-button--outline" aria-pressed="false">LIST</button>
</div>

<!-- The action row: inline-end, one primary -->
<div class="nib-action-row">
  <button type="button" class="nib-button nib-button--ghost" aria-keyshortcuts="Escape">
    <span class="nib-button__key" aria-hidden="true">[ESC]</span><span class="nib-button__word">CANCEL</span>
  </button>
  <button type="button" class="nib-button nib-button--ghost">DISCARD</button>
  <button type="button" class="nib-button nib-button--outline" disabled>ARCHIVE</button>
  <button type="button" class="nib-button nib-button--destructive">DELETE</button>
  <button type="button" class="nib-button nib-button--outline">PREVIEW</button>
  <button type="submit" class="nib-button nib-button--primary">SAVE</button>
</div>`;

const code = {
  html,
  react: `<button type="button" className="nib-button nib-button--ghost" aria-keyshortcuts="Escape">
  <span className="nib-button__key" aria-hidden="true">[ESC]</span>
  <span className="nib-button__word">CANCEL</span>
</button>
<button type="submit" className="nib-button nib-button--primary">SAVE</button>`,
  vue: `<button type="button" class="nib-button nib-button--ghost" aria-keyshortcuts="Escape">
  <span class="nib-button__key" aria-hidden="true">[ESC]</span>
  <span class="nib-button__word">CANCEL</span>
</button>
<button type="submit" class="nib-button nib-button--primary">SAVE</button>`,
  svelte: `<button type="button" class="nib-button nib-button--ghost" aria-keyshortcuts="Escape">
  <span class="nib-button__key" aria-hidden="true">[ESC]</span>
  <span class="nib-button__word">CANCEL</span>
</button>
<button type="submit" class="nib-button nib-button--primary">SAVE</button>`,
};
---

<ComponentPage
  title="Button"
  lead="Words first: a mono verb, and hierarchy by stroke weight. Primary 2px, outline 1px, ghost none."
  kind="CSS"
  code={code}
>
  <div slot="example" class="docs-stack" set:html={html} />
  <h2>Usage</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>nib-button--primary</code>: 2px ink frame, transparent ground. <strong>One per view</strong>: it is the only
      2px frame on screen.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>nib-button--outline</code>: 1px line border. <code>aria-pressed="true"</code> makes it a cursor block.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>nib-button--ghost</code>: no visible border, hover fill only; for low-priority actions in dense rows.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>nib-button--destructive</code>: red text and a 1px red border.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>nib-button--destructive nib-button--primary</code>: the confirm button of a destructive dialog (
      <code>DELETE PROJECT</code>). It takes the primary's place, so the view still has one 2px frame.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>nib-button--lg</code>: 36px, for page-level calls to action. On touch screens every button is at least 44px
      and the primary 48px.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Placement.</strong> The primary sits in its region's action row (<code>nib-action-row</code>): the footer of
    a form, dialog, sheet or pane, at the inline end, or next to the headline in a hero. Pressed toggles and option
    pickers live in the header or content; a primary never shares a row with a cursor block.
  </p>
  <p>
    Text is a verb (<code>SAVE</code>, <code>ADD TO CART</code>). An icon may sit before the word; the word stays. Print
    a keyboard shortcut before the word in <code>nib-button__key</code>, and declare it with
    <code>aria-keyshortcuts</code>.
  </p>
  <ul slot="accessibility">
    <li>
      A native <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> (or <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> for navigation): Enter and Space work, and the
      word is the accessible name.
    </li>
    <li>
      Toggles use <code>aria-pressed</code>; screen readers announce "pressed". The cursor block is drawn from that
      attribute, so it cannot show without it.
    </li>
    <li>
      The printed shortcut is <code>aria-hidden</code>; <code>aria-keyshortcuts</code> carries it to assistive
      technology. Write it per platform (<code>[⌘↵]</code> / <code>Meta+Enter</code> on macOS,
      <code>[CTRL↵]</code> / <code>Control+Enter</code> elsewhere). A single printable character needs a modifier, or it
      fires on speech input (WCAG 2.1.4); keys such as Escape are fine alone.
    </li>
    <li>
      Prefer <code>disabled</code> on native buttons; use <code>aria-disabled="true"</code> to keep it focusable.
    </li>
    <li>Focus is a 2px accent outline, 2px off the border; in forced colours it uses the system colours.</li>
  </ul>
</ComponentPage>

<style>
  .docs-stack {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--nib-space-lg);
  }
</style>
